<title>USA: Cincinnati Bell Q1 shr $0.83 after credits.</title>
<headline>Cincinnati Bell Q1 shr $0.83 after credits.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>CINCINNATI BELL INC.</p>
<p>	   Revenues, Net Income and Earnings Per Common Share</p>
<p>		   In Millions, Except Per Share Amounts</p>
<p>				 (Unaudited)</p>
<p>					     For the Three Months</p>
<p>						Ended March 31,</p>
<p>						 1997	1996  % Change</p>
<p> Revenues				  $429.5    $362.1     19</p>
<p> Net Income(a)			     57.2	41.7     37</p>
<p> Earnings Per Common Share(a)	  0.83	0.62     34</p>
<p>Weighted Avg. Number of</p>
<p> Common Shares Outstanding(000)    68,775    66,872	3</p>
<p>(a) Includes special credits, which totaled $15 million in the first quarter of 1997 and $5.5 million in the first quarter of 1996.  Those credits increased net income by $9.6 million, or 14 cents per share in the first quarter of 1997, and $3.5 million, or 5 cents per share in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
